<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n103905" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίη</span></b> , better <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τί ἢ</span></b>  (<i><span class="en">
			A.D.
			<u>Conj.</u>
			255.8
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			256.3
		</span></i>), 
			Att.
		 (?) <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τιή</span></b>  (v. infr.),
		strengthd. form of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τί</span>; <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>why? wherefore?</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				1.365
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				6.145
			</span></i>,al., <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				35
			</span></i>, and 
				Att.
			 Comedy: folld. by a Particle, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίη
				δὲ . . </span>; <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				6.55
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				15.244
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				16.421
			</span></i>, al.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίη δὴ . . </span>; <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				21.436
			</span></i>; doubled, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τιὴ τί δή</span>;
			standing alone, <i>why so, tell me?</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>V.</u>
				1155
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Pax</u>
				1018
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Th.</u>
				84
			</span></i>. (The oxyt. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τιή</span> is called 
				Att.
			 by <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				118.36
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				45.4
			</span></i>, but was unknown to <i><span class="en">
				A.D.
			</span></i> and is prob. a fiction; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίη</span>
			and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τιὴ</span> are dub. ll. in <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				826
			</span></i>; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					1.2
				</span></i>
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁτιή</span>.)</div>
